@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@* The landing page's frame: the page itself and nothing around it.

   The landing page is public marketing, and the design draws it with a header and a footer of its
   own rather than inside the application's sidebar - so it is the one screen that does not sit in
   MainLayout's shell. The page brings its own header, language switch and way in.

   FR-13: the page's failures pass through the one boundary, as every screen in MainLayout's do.

   The connection dock stays, for the reason MainLayout keeps it outside its grid: it belongs to the
   circuit rather than to any screen, and the landing page runs on a circuit like every other. *@

<SessionExpiryBoundary>
    @Body
</SessionExpiryBoundary>

<DtConnectionDock />
